# countdown: prints 54321
#
# Row 0 seeds the counter and drops the eye into the loop. The turn at (1,0)
# sets the heading south, so the cell it lands on -- (1,1) -- must turn it east
# again before the body runs: headings persist until a triangle changes them.
#
# Row 1 is the loop body and is exactly as wide as the plate, so running off the
# east edge wraps straight back to its own start. The guard at x=0 is the exit:
# once the decremented counter reaches zero it turns south into row 2, which is
# void, and the machine halts.
#
# Composition: every cell the eye never visits is a PUSH disc that never
# executes, its scale a horizontal swell. Void
# padding cannot carry a swell (a void draws nothing and must have scale 0),
# so the padding was replaced. Ground is 6 throughout. No form, no
# variant and no reachable scale changed.
#
#
# Ends with a newline: push 1, push_acc 2 makes 10, then OUT_CHAR.
%plate 7x3

o156  v156  o156  o176  o156  o126  o1.6
v326  >146  %166  +176  o116  #266  %146
>1.6  o116  o226  +2.6  ...6  o126  o1.6
